course: dictionary
lesson: 14812
title: Who is chasing whom?
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A pursuer is someone who chases another person or animal to try to catch them. The word comes from pursue, which means to follow closely behind. Look for clues like chase, run, hunt or escape to spot a pursuer in a story.
explain: «The thief dashed down the street, and the police officer ran after him.» The thief is running away, so he is being chased. The police officer is the pursuer, because she is the one trying to catch him.
explain: A pursuer is a noun, so it can be a person or an animal. Ask yourself: who is running away, and who is coming after them? The one coming after them is the pursuer. «The hero hid behind a rock to shake off his pursuers.» Hiding behind a rock is a way to lose them.
fact: A pursuer is someone who is chasing or following another person or animal to catch them.
fact: «The hero hid from his pursuers in the old barn.» The pursuers are the people trying to find him.
fact: In nature, a predator is the pursuer of its prey: «The cheetah is a fast pursuer of the antelope.»
fact: Useful phrases: «escape from pursuers», «shake off a pursuer» (lose them), and «in hot pursuit» (chasing very closely).
fact: One pursuer is a pursuer; more than one are pursuers.
exercise: «The fox ran fast, with the hunting dogs as its pursuers.» Who is chasing the fox? | *The hunting dogs | The farmer's cows | The birds in the trees | The fox's own tail
exercise: Ella says a pursuer is a kind of pet. What is a pursuer really? | A person who runs for fun | A tiny, soft animal | A type of shoe | *Someone who chases another to catch them
exercise: What does «in hot pursuit» mean? | Sleeping soundly | *Chasing very closely | Hiding from everyone | Singing loudly
test: «The thief escaped from his pursuers by running into the woods.» What did the thief do? | *Ran away from the people chasing him | Went to sleep under a tree | Stayed still and waited for them | Shook hands with his pursuers
test: Which word means someone who chases another to catch them? | purchaser | purse | parent | *pursuer
exam: «The cheetah was the pursuer, and the gazelle ran for its life.» Who was chasing? | The gazelle | The sun | *The cheetah | The grass
